  "notes": "⛔ **The no-samples entry.** Khayree's documented style is \"similar to the G-Funk… but usually without the use of samples\", so the entire harmony is played on synths — which makes this the only Bay model here whose chords are authored as real progressions with a modulation-friendly four-chord reach rather than as an implied riff, and the only one at \"medium note density\" instead of low. Four played layers (bass, pad, lead, counter-line) put `countermelody.densityRatio` at 0.5 and the counter above the lead. Synth bass with slides between roots is the highest `glideProb` in the batch at 0.75, over a drier, more synthetic programmed kit — the model's `quantizeStrength` is 0.9, the tightest of the Bay group, because a drum machine playing itself is not a live drummer. ⚠ No `drums.bass808` here, unlike E-40, The Click and C-Bo: the research says the kick is 808-layered and the synth bass is \"deep and forward, tuned for trunk response\", which is one played low layer with a reinforced kick, not the two-lane split those three describe. ⚠ `medium`: the research rates the production idiom medium-high and the artist medium, and the INFERRED parameter is everything downstream of \"multiple synth layers… all played\" — the register split between those layers is not documented anywhere.",
